---
source: crates/peekbuddy-viewer/src/watches/tests.rs
expression: table
---
Arming
  label:   Arming
  icon:    Dots
  tooltip: PeekBuddy is opening this folder. It becomes Live as soon as changes are being received.
Live
  label:   Live
  icon:    Dot
  tooltip: Changes in this folder are being recorded.
Overflowed
  label:   Overflowed
  icon:    Triangle
  tooltip: Windows reported more changes than PeekBuddy's buffer could hold. A gap is recorded and a scan of the folder follows to find what was missed.
Reconciling
  label:   Reconciling
  icon:    Cycle
  tooltip: PeekBuddy is scanning the folder to find what changed during a gap. Rows found by the scan are marked as reconcile results.
SuspendedByUser
  label:   Paused
  icon:    Pause
  tooltip: Paused by you. The watch stays armed, changes are counted but not recorded. Resume to record again.
SuspendedQueryRemove
  label:   Suspended (drive removal)
  icon:    Lock
  tooltip: The drive is being removed. PeekBuddy let go of the folder and watches it again when the drive is back.
Lost
  label:   Lost
  icon:    Cross
  tooltip: The folder is gone or cannot be reached. PeekBuddy keeps trying and records when it is back.
Restored
  label:   Restored
  icon:    Check
  tooltip: The folder is back. PeekBuddy scans it to find what changed while it was gone; then the watch is Live again.
SuspendedLocked
  label:   Suspended (drive locked)
  icon:    Lock
  tooltip: The drive is locked or being checked. PeekBuddy waits and arms the watch again when the drive is available.
not armed yet
  label:   Starts after restart
  icon:    Clock
  tooltip: Saved. This folder is recorded once PeekBuddy's engine has restarted.
